          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong coverage
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            consists of, for each object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\in C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i \colon U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} target
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            to be thought of as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} covering families
            = succeed ".\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} pullback
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          %p
            One of the main purposes of a coverage is that it provides the minimum structure necessary to define a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            (or more generally
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            is defined to be the category of sheaves (of sets) on a small site. From this perspective, the example to keep in mind is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            of open sets in some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \hookrightarrow U\}
            is a covering family iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \bigcup_i U_i
          %p
            Another perspective on a coverage is that the covering families are “postulated well-behaved quotients.” That is, saying that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
            is a covering family means that we want to think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            as a well-behaved quotient (i.e. colimit) of the
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            may or may not
            %em actually
            be a colimit of the
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+coverage"} subcanonical
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            into its category of sheaves is “the free cocompletion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that takes covering families to well-behaved quotients”; compare how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            of an arbitrary category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            into its category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
            is its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
          %p
            The traditional name for a coverage, with the extra saturation conditions imposed, is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
            %em coverage
            for a pullback-stable system of covering families and
            %em Grothendieck coverage
            if the extra saturation conditions are imposed. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            for a discussion of the objections to that term.
          %p
            A related notion is that of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+for+a+Grothendieck+topology"} basis for a Grothendieck topology
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          %h2#Definition Definition
          #ConditionsOnACoverage.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong coverage
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              consists of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              assigning to each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\in C
              a collection of families of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
                  families
            %ul
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
                is a covering family and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:V\to U
                is a morphism, then there exists a covering family
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{h_j:V_j\to V\}
                such that each composite
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g h_j
                factors through some
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi h
                                      %mi j
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mo
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi f
                                      %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    V_j &amp;\overset{k}{\longrightarrow}&amp; U_i
                    \\\
                    \\mathllap{{}^{h_j}}\big\downarrow &amp; &amp; \big\downarrow\mathrlap{^{f_i}}
                    \\\
                    V &amp;\underset{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; U
                    }
                    \\;\;.
            %p
              (NB. The logic here is:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi h
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall f, \forall g, \exists h, \forall j, \exists i, \exists k \colon
              such that the above
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              is a category equipped with a coverage.
          %p
            Often
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+site"} large site
            for complications that may otherwise arise.
          %h3#sheaves_on_a_site Sheaves on a site
          %p
            See
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
            is a family of morphisms with codomain
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X:C^{op}\to Set
            is called a
            %strong sheaf
            for this family if
          %ul
            %li
              For any collection of elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i \in X(U_i)
              such that, whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:V\to U_i
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:V\to U_j
              are such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mi g
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi j
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i g = f_j h
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(g)(x_i) = X(h)(x_j)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X(U)
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(f_i)(x)=x_i
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a site, a presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X:C^{op}\to Set
            is called a
            %strong sheaf
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            if it is a sheaf for every covering family in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+coverage"} subcanonical
            if every representable functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(-,c):C^{op}\to Set
            is a sheaf.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            is a full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set]
            of presheaves. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+coverage"} subcanonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to [C^{op},Set]
            factors through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is small, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set]
            and a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
          %h3#cartesian Sites with pullbacks
          %p
            If, as is frequently the case,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullbacks
          %ul
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
              is a covering family and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:V\to U
              is a morphism, then the family of pullbacks
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{g^*(f_i):g^*U_i\to V\}
              is a covering family of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            One can also impose the weaker condition that the pullbacks of covering families exist and are covering families, even if not all pullbacks exist in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %strong cartesian coverage
          %p
            Likewise, when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has pullbacks (of covering families), the condition for a presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be a sheaf for a covering family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
            can be stated more simply (and probably more familiarly, to some readers), as the assertion that the following diagram is an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇉
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X(U) \to \prod_{i\in I} X(U_i) \rightrightarrows \prod_{j,k\in I} X(U_j\times_U U_k).
          %p
            The generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stacks
            using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+object"} cosimplicial objects
            is then straightforward.
          %h3#saturation_conditions Saturation conditions
          %p The collection of covering families can be “closed up” under a number of convenient operations without changing the notion of sheaf.
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Any presheaf is a sheaf for the singleton family
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi U
                        %mo :
                        %mi U
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1_U:U\to U\}
            %li
              %p
                Any presheaf which is a sheaf for a family
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
                and also for some family
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi J
                            %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{h_{i j}:U_{i j} \to U_i\}_{j\in J_i}
                for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                is also a sheaf for the family of all composites
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi J
                              %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i h_{i j}:U_{i j}\to U\}_{i\in I, j\in J_i}
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                be a site and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
                a covering family, and suppose
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{g_j:V_j\to U\}_{j\in J}
                is a family of morphisms such that each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
                factors through some
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_j
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is also a sheaf for the family
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mi j
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi j
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{g_j:V_j\to U\}_{j\in J}
                %em
                  (NB: for this condition, it is essential that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i\}
                  be part of a coverage and that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  be a sheaf for the entire coverage, not just for
                  = succeed ".)" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i\}
            %li
              %p
                For any family
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
                it generates is the family of all morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:V\to U
                which factor through some
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a sheaf for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i\}
                iff it is a sheaf for the sieve it generates.
          %h3#grothendieck_coverages Grothendieck coverages
          %p Grothendieck originally considered only coverages that are closed under some or all of the above saturation conditions.
          %p
            Because of the final condition, we may choose to consider only covering
            = succeed "." do
              %em sieves
            %strong Grothendieck coverage
            (commonly called a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            = succeed "," do
              %em covering sieves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a sieve on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:V\to U
            is a morphism, we define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^*(R)
            to be the sieve on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            consisting of all morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g h
            factors through some morphism in
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a covering sieve on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:V\to U
                is any morphism, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^*(R)
                is a covering sieve on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %li
              %p
                For each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                the sieve
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_U
                consisting of
                %em all
                morphisms into
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                (the sieve generated by the singleton family
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1_U\}
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a covering sieve on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is an arbitrary sieve on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                such that for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:V\to U
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(S)
                is a covering sieve on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is also a covering sieve on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            One can then show that for every coverage, there is a
            %em unique
            Grothendieck coverage having the same sheaves. When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is small, then Grothendieck coverages on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are also in bijective correspondence with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topologies
            on its presheaf topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtopos"} subtoposes
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set]
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
          %p
            On the other hand, it is often useful to consider only pullback-stable covering families, without needing to close them up into sieves satisfying the saturation conditions. For instance, in many cases the generating covering families will be finite and easy to describe. As we saw above, the notion of sheaf can also be defined more explicitly in terms of covering families, especially when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has pullbacks.
          %p
            Frequently, though, these covering families will satisfy at least some of the saturation conditions. The name
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+pretopology"} Grothendieck pretopology
            or
            %em basis for a Grothendieck topology
            is commonly used for a coverage (often of the stronger sort requiring pullbacks) that also satisfies
          %ul
            %li
              %p Every isomorphism is a covering family.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i\to U\}_{i\in I}
                is a covering family and for each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi J
                              %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{h_{i j}:U_{i j} \to U_i\}_{j\in J_i}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i h_{i j}:U_{i j}\to U\}_{i\in I, j\in U_i}
                is also a covering family.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Op(X)
                its
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+coverage"} subcanonical
                coverage on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Op
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Op(X)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
                is a collection of further open subsets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}
                such that their union (in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∪
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cup_i U_i = U
              %p
                This is the standard choice of coverage on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Op
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Op(X)
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+for+the+topology"} basis for the topology
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is also a coverage on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Op(X)
                is intersection of open subsets). Notice that thence a basis for a topology on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is not what is called a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+for+a+Grothendieck+topology"} basis for a Grothendieck topology
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Op
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Op(X)
            %li
              %p
                Similarly on (any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
                version of) the category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                or
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
                or similar categories of topological spaces possibly with extra
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} structure
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              %p
                Another choice of coverage is given by taking covering families to consist of
                = succeed "s," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+map"} étale map
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
                consist of local homeomorphisms and in addition gives the local homeomorphism out of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_i U_i \to X
            %li
              %p
                On
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
                also
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
                = succeed "While" do
                  %br/
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            %li
              %p
                There are many interesting coverages on the category of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} schemes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fpqc+topology"} fpqc topology
            %li
              %p
                On any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                there is the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+coverage"} trivial coverage
                which has no covering families at all. Every presheaf is a sheaf for this coverage (and in particular, it is subcanonical). The corresponding Grothendieck coverage consists of all sieves that contain a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+epimorphism"} split epimorphism
            %li
              %p
                On any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
                there is a coverage, called the
                = succeed "," do
                  %em regular coverage
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f:V\to U\}
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
            %li
              %p
                On any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
                there is a a coverage, called the
                = succeed "," do
                  %em coherent coverage
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi i
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i:U_i \to U\}_{1\le i\le n}
                the union of whose images is all of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %em geometric coverage
                on any infinitary-coherent category.
            %li
              %p
                On any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
                there is a coverage, called the
                = succeed "," do
                  %em extensive coverage
            %li
              %p
                Any category has a
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coverage"} canonical coverage
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong universally effective-epimorphic
            %li
              %p
                The canonical coverage on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
                coincides with its geometric coverage, and moreover every sheaf for this coverage is representable. That is, a Grothendieck topos is a (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+site"}> large
                ) site which is equivalent to its own category of sheaves.
          %h2#applications Applications
          %p
            In addition to the construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stacks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The definition of internal
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctors
            %li
              %p
                The construction of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folk+model+structure"} model structures for internal categories
          %h2#in_higher_category_theory In higher category theory
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            and hence that of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+pretopology"} Grothendieck pretopology
            and coverage typically has its straightforward analogs in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %p
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            the corresponding notion is that of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            = succeed "-site" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of this in terms of localization at a coverage is at…
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"}> open cover
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+cover"} closed cover
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-net"} quasi-net
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
                , especially section C2.1.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://home.imf.au.dk/kock/postulated.pdf"} Postulated colimits and left exactness of Kan-extensions
        .revisedby
          %p
